      "writtenOn": "2020-10-13T16:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the 2.18 upgrade blocked on making these changes to support (or emulate) the new gen_mod_rs behavior? It seems like the default behavior in 2.18 hasn\u0027t changed.\n\nMy (possibly incorrect) understanding of the gen_mod_rs option from looking at [1] and [2] is that it\u0027s meant to allow including code generated from multiple proto definitions via a single mod.rs file.\n\nThis isn\u0027t something we support right now as we only accept a single proto definition per rust_protobuf module. We could probably support multiple generated files in the future if there\u0027s demand for it, but I think properly supporting that should be a separate effort as we\u0027d need to make sure it works for all SourceProvider modules.\n\n[1] https://github.com/stepancheg/rust-protobuf/commit/a9f694aaf0f6802d10dec0d453831a88ca6c595c\n[2] https://github.com/stepancheg/rust-protobuf/pull/525",
